From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: FAROVITUS <farovitus@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 20:33:58 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fsgen: install lib and lib64 copies at their literal path

My device keeps its vendor blobs in the system image, and its blob list
copies some of them to both lib/ and lib64/. fsgen turns each copy into a
generated prebuilt module, and for lib/ and lib64/ it picks a module type
that builds both arch variants and puts the 64-bit one in lib64/, so the
two copies of one blob collide with each other and the build stops.

Install copies into lib/ and lib64/ with prebuilt_any at the literal
destination path instead. Every Lineage 22.2 zeroflte ROM I built had
this change; I made it in the build tree on 2026-11-11 and it was never
saved anywhere else until now.

Signed-off-by: FAROVITUS <farovitus@gmail.com>
---
diff --git a/fsgen/prebuilt_etc_modules_gen.go b/fsgen/prebuilt_etc_modules_gen.go
index e4bb07c..27581bb 100644
--- a/fsgen/prebuilt_etc_modules_gen.go
+++ b/fsgen/prebuilt_etc_modules_gen.go
@@ -304,6 +304,16 @@ func createPrebuiltEtcModulesInDirectory(ctx android.LoadHookContext, partition,
 	moduleFactory := etcInstallPathToFactoryList[etcInstallPathKey]
 	relDestDirFromInstallDirBase, _ := filepath.Rel(etcInstallPathKey, destDir)
 
+	// A copy into lib/ or lib64/ installs one file at that exact path. The
+	// bitcode module type builds both arch variants and puts the 64-bit one
+	// in lib64/, so a blob copied to both lib/ and lib64/ (common on devices
+	// whose vendor files live in the system image) collides with itself.
+	// Install these with prebuilt_any at the literal destination instead.
+	if etcInstallPathKey == "lib" || etcInstallPathKey == "lib64" {
+		moduleFactory = etc.PrebuiltAnyFactory
+		relDestDirFromInstallDirBase = destDir
+	}
+
 	for fileIndex := range maxLen {
 		srcTuple := []srcBaseFileInstallBaseFileTuple{}
 		for _, srcFile := range android.SortedKeys(groupedDestFiles) {
-- 
